  "definition": "A spacecraft battery stores electrical energy for launch, eclipse, contingencies and demands above the generating source's instantaneous capability. Its nameplate capacity is only one design input. Voltage, permissible current, temperature, usable depth of discharge (DoD), ageing, protection and the required cycle life determine what the spacecraft can use.[^1]",
